-- Alignment of Uldaman and Upper Blackrock Spire with the sniff-based reference: 12 extra Stonevault Pillagers removed,
--   three bosses moved to their sniffed spots.
-- What a player sees today: Uldaman holds 12 Stonevault Pillagers (24830, elite) that neither the Cataclysm Preservation sniff
--   database nor the SkyFire 5.4.8 database spawns anywhere on the map (several sit on top of the normal Stonevault packs).
--   In Blackrock Spire (map 229) Quartermaster Zigris stands 22 yards, Halycon 17 yards and Mother Smolderweb 27 yards away
--   from the spot where both references place them.
-- Cause: the Pillager spawns come from an unrelated source (no counterpart in either reference); the three boss positions
--   come from an older database.
-- Checked: both references (cpp guids 45749, 40245, 44342 = sf guids, identical rows) agree on the positions; the 12 Pillagers
--   (guids 320803,320961,320965,320967,320968,320970,321004,321005,321006,321007,321010,321011) have no formation, pool, game
--   event, linked respawn, waypoint, condition or quest relation, only a plain creature_addon row and the template SmartAI
--   (Enrage / Flee), and no C++ script mentions the entry. The three bosses are stationary (MovementType 0, no path, no
--   formation, pool, event, linked respawn, smart script or condition); boss_quartermaster_zigris.cpp, boss_halycon.cpp (only the
--   Gizrul summon point, not the boss) and boss_mother_smolderweb.cpp contain no fixed positions.
-- Change: DELETE the 12 Pillager spawns and their creature_addon rows; UPDATE position and orientation of Zigris (322826),
--   Halycon (322616) and Mother Smolderweb (322477) to the reference values.
-- Left alone on purpose: Wyrmthalak (script summon points sit at the current spot), Solakar Flamewreath and Gizrul (no reference
--   spawn, but nothing else spawns Solakar, and Gizrul has its own 7-point path), High Examiner Tae'thelan (quest giver 27679/27680),
--   Ancient Stone Keeper and Revelosh (patrol paths, the "move" is only the path start).
-- Source: Cataclysm Preservation sniff database and SkyFire 5.4.8 database (comparison), 18-11-2026.
-- Rollback (the rows and values before this update):
